{title: Seled Without Children}
{subtitle: 1 Chronicles 2:30; 2:25–31; 2:3–5}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 81}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [C] | [Bb] | [Dm] [C] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Sons of Ju[Dm]dah, line [C]by line
Er, [Bb]Onan, and She[Dm]lah shine
[C]Bath-shua gave [Bb]these three
[Dm]The firstborn Er [C]was not seen
By [F]the Lord [C/E]with [Dm]favor, no
[Bb]His path [C]ended, [Dm]it is so
[Bb]Tamar [C]bore Perez [Dm]and Zerah
Judah had five [C]sons, no fear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Perez gave Hezron, Ha[Dm]mul
Hezron's first[Bb]born, Ram the [C]full
Bunah, O[F]ren, [C/E]Ozem, [Dm]Ahijah
[Bb]Ram's sons: Maaz, Ja[C]min, Eker
[Dm]Jerahmeel had Atarah too
[Bb]She was Onam's [C]mother, true
Shammai [F]and Ja[C/E]da, On[Dm]am's seed
[Bb]Nadab and Abis[C]hur, indeed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[F]Abishur's [C/E]wife, Abi[Dm]hail
Bore [Bb]Ahban and [C]Molid, faithful
[F]Nadab's sons, [C/E]two names [Dm]here
[Bb]Seled [C]and Ap[Dm]paim, [Bb]so clear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Seled [C]died with[Dm]out [Bb]children
His [C]line stopped, his sto[F]ry end[C/E]ed
Ap[Dm]paim walked on ahead
[Bb]Ishi, [C]Sheshan, Ahlai [F]fed
[C/E]A re[Dm]cord kept in Chron[Bb]icles
Names [C]preserved, not [Bb]forgot[C]ten
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Jerahmeel's [Dm]clan, Ju[Bb]dah's part
His[C]tory after the [F]exi[C/E]le's art
Who lived, [Dm]who died, who [Bb]stayed
The [C]genealogy, [F]the weight
[C/E]Seled's life, [Dm]brief[Bb]ly known
[C]Without children, [F]a[C/E]lone
But the [Dm]book holds his [Bb]name
In the [C]tribe, same as [Dm]flame
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Seled died [Bb]without chil[C]dren
His line stopped, [F]his sto[C/E]ry end[Dm]ed
Appaim walked [Bb]on a[C]head
Ishi, Sheshan, [F]Ah[C/E]lai fed
[Dm]A record kept [Bb]in Chronicles
[C]Names preser[Bb]ved, not [C]forgot[Dm]ten
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Seled died [C]without children [Bb]
Re[C]membered in the text
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
